%S A123404 1,2,4,11,32,136,749,6142,71759,1174550,25734030,732572210,26561326323
%N A123404 Number of alternately colorable perfect graphs on n nodes.
%C A123404 A graph is alternately colorable if its edges can be colored with two colors so that the colors alternate around every chordless cycle of length at least 4. Every alternately colorable graph is perfect: such a graph can contain no odd hole and no odd antihole. - _Meghanto Majumder_, Sep 28 2026
